WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.920
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.040
Today, we have the final episode
in our series on Ozempic

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.960
and we ask what’s a safer and cheaper
way to lose weight than GLP-1 drugs?

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.237
Can we drug our way
out of the obesity crisis?

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.640
Are these GLP-1 drugs the answer
to the obesity epidemic?

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.080
The head of
the European Association

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.720
for the Study of Obesity
was pretty bullish,

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.840
conveniently failing to disclose
that his group had received

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.200
millions of dollars
from the drug maker.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.320
But doesn’t getting
a tiny weekly injection

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.200
sound far easier than getting
all sweaty in the gym?

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.600
Do these game-changing
new medications

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.600
"make lifestyle-based treatment
of obesity obsolete"?

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.360
Let’s ask those paid by
the two main GLP-1 drug makers,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.200
which now have
a combined net worth

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.440
greater than a trillion dollars.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.520
The World Obesity Federation,

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.280
which evidently just got
a million dollars

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.880
from the Ozempic company,

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.440
published a consensus statement
in one of its journals

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.600
favoring the definition
of obesity as a disease.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.920
This designation
may not benefit patients,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.000
but it will benefit doctors
and drug companies

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.920
when health insurance
and clinical guidelines

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.320
promote treatment
with drugs and surgery.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.680
A concern is that labeling
obesity as a disease

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.440
risks reducing our autonomy,

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.240
disempowering and robbing us
of the intrinsic motivation

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.160
that’s an important enabler
of change.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.680
It encourages fatalism,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.280
promoting the fallacy
that genetics are destiny.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.480
But, of course,
it can’t be our genes.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.120
The obesity epidemic only
started a few decades ago.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.520
Our genes didn’t somehow
magically change

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.440
in the late 1970s.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.000
Others blame lack of willpower,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.840
but that doesn’t make
any sense either.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.760
All of us coincidentally lost
our collective self-control?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.480
It’s the food.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.320
The rise in the number
of excess calories

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.840
provided by the U.S. food supply

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.920
is more than sufficient
to explain the obesity epidemic.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.560
Obesity is not
some moral failing.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.400
The battle of the bulge is
a battle against biology.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.560
We’re living
in a toxic food environment,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.400
drowning in a sea
of excess calories,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.680
being bombarded with ads
for fast food and candy.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.280
Becoming overweight is
a normal, natural response

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.480
to the abnormal,
unnatural ubiquity

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.760
of sugary, fatty foods that are
concentrated with calories.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.160
So, the prime cause
for the obesity epidemic

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.800
is neither gluttony nor sloth.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.320
Being overweight may simply be

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.160
a normal response,
by normal people,

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.400
to an abnormal situation.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.040
And with nearly three-quarters
of Americans overweight,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.280
it’s literally normal.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.760
So, if obesity is
to be understood

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.840
as "normal physiology within
a pathological environment,"

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.240
there is an argument
that drugs like Ozempic

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.840
really aren’t tackling
the root cause of obesity.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.320
These drugs will likely have
only a modest effect

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.560
on reducing
the rapidly growing epidemic

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.800
and may even make it worse,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.640
as Big Pharma and its lobbyists

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.280
try to shift society’s focus
to drugs

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.400
rather than broader
public health strategies.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.600
The real solution would involve
fixing the food system,

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.600
but why would Big Food
change its ways

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.080
if obesity can be treated
with drugs?

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.600
So, the main actors responsible
for creating and perpetuating

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.240
the obesity-generating world
will continue undisturbed.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.440
England’s health secretary
was keen to use GLP-1 drugs

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.200
as a "way of preventing illness

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.320
without resorting
to ’nanny state’ measures,"

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.800
but advocates are just
talking about things like

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.240
restricting the thousands of ads
kids see every year

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.440
for candy, liquid candy
(soft drinks),

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.880
breakfast candy, and fast food.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.160
A quarter century ago,

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.000
the term "Social Determinants
of Health" was coined,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.960
defined as the nonmedical
factors that influence health

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.520
too often ignored
by the medical establishment,

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:04.800
such as poverty.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.440
They explain why the top
1 percent, for example,

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.000
live about 10 to 15 years longer
than the bottom 1 percent.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
More recently,
based on experience

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.760
with the alcohol
and tobacco industries,

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.400
the concept of "Commercial
Determinants of Health"

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.280
was introduced,

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.560
which can be defined as
"factors that influence health

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.440
which stem from the profit
motive," also referred to

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.760
as the Corporate
Determinants of Health.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.000
The food and beverage sectors
spend huge amounts

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.760
on developing
and marketing products

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.280
packed with sugar,
fat, and salt,

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:36.080
deliberately designed
to lead to addictive consumption

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.000
that contributes
to the increasing prevalence

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.840
of chronic disease.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.200
Public corporations like
Coca-Cola have a legal duty

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.160
to maximize return
to their shareholders,

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.440
and those running the companies

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.080
are heavily incentivized
to achieve this.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.320
Many observers are outraged
by stories

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:55.680
of what some of these companies
do to maximize returns,

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.200
but as people working in the
tobacco industry can testify,

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.400
being the subject
of widespread disrepute

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.720
is more than offset
by the financial rewards.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.200
And psychological defense
mechanisms can take care

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.120
of any residual unease about
contributing to the suffering

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:16.080
and death of fellow humans whom
they do not personally know.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.720
The greatest challenge
to improving health may lie

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:19.840
in the tension between

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.200
wealth creation
and health creation.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.440
Introducing a temporary
weight-loss fix

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.920
using GLP-1 drugs like Ozempic,

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.080
without consideration
of their wider implications

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.120
and a long-term plan,

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:35.200
has been likened to sprinkling
water on a raging blaze.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.000
The war against obesity
cannot be won without measures

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.640
to prevent obesity
in the first place.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.040
That means tackling
the food environment,

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.480
which is based on high-calorie,
fatty, salty, sugary junk,

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.920
rather than relying
on medication

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:51.600
as a "damage limitation
exercise."

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:55.040
Yeah, but limiting damage
is a good thing.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.280
Sure, these drugs may not make
much of a dent

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.800
on a population scale,

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.360
but what about
on an individual basis?

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.600
It’d be great if people ate
healthfully enough

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.200
to prevent and treat
heart disease,

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.200
high blood pressure,
and diabetes too,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.720
but until that happens,

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.480
drugs for those conditions
can literally be life saving.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:16.400
Obesity so dramatically
decreases one’s lifespan--

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.040
reducing life expectancy
as much as a decade--

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.560
that these GLP-1 drugs--
like bariatric surgery--

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.880
should be considered
as a last resort

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.520
for those unwilling
or unable to treat

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.920
the cause of their obesity.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.440
Put diabetics on Ozempic,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.320
and they eat less
high-fat and sweet foods.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:35.840
Put nondiabetics on Ozempic,

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.320
and they eat less high-fat
and non-sweet foods.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.840
So, diabetics on Ozempic

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:41.760
are eating fewer
pastries and doughnuts,

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.440
and nondiabetics on Ozempic

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.400
are eating fewer ham, cheese,
and sausage sandwiches.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.240
The problem
is people eat too much crap;

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.480
so, anything that gets people
to eat less crap

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.440
can be beneficial,

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.400
including surgically rearranging
our digestive organs

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.320
with bariatric surgery.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.000
But we don’t need
to go under the knife

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.000
or take a $1,000-a-month drug
to de-crap our diet.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.160
But what about the cravings,
though?

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:07.840
The obesogenic environment--

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.960
that is, the obesity-generating
toxic food environment--

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.200
can overwhelm
even substantial efforts

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.000
to enact individual
behavioral changes.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.040
After ramping up for three
months to high-dose Ozempic,

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.360
people are able
to cut nearly 1,000 calories

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.640
out of their daily diet.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.360
How could you possibly do that
without drugs,

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:26.320
unless you were on some kind

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.480
of liquid diet
meal-replacement shakes

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.520
or something?

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.280
Or, you could eat
a diet centered around

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.280
the healthiest foods
on the planet.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:38.560
If you put people on a diet
packed with fruits, vegetables,

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.760
whole grains, and beans,

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.320
and allow them to eat
as much as they want,

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:46.240
they end up eating about
50 percent fewer calories

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.760
than they might have otherwise.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.560
Just as full,
on half the calories.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.200
Wait. How can people be
satisfied after cutting

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.080
more than 1,000 calories
out of their daily diets?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:59.600
By eating more high-bulk,
low-calorie-density foods

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.480
(vegetables, fruits,
whole grains, and beans)

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.000
and fewer calorie-dense foods,

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.880
like meats, cheeses,
sugars, and fats.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.520
No wonder a whole food
plant-based diet apparently

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:13.680
achieved greater weight loss
than any other diet.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.680
So, could good nutrition present
a safer and cheaper approach

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.920
to weight loss
for most patients?

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.080
Not only can the ingestion
of a plant-based meal

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.840
more than double
GLP-1 secretion,

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.600
compared to
a same-calorie meat meal,

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.760
but plant-based diets
can also cause weight loss

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:30.720
by virtue of calorie-trapping,
high-fiber foods,

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.080
which flush calories away,

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.240
or by boosting
our resting metabolic rate,

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.200
which helps explain

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.760
why the largest study
of vegans to date

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.680
showed that those eating
strictly plant-based diets

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.400
are about 35 pounds (16 kg)
lighter, on average.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.800
One randomized trial found
that a strictly plant-based diet

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.720
may reduce annual food costs
by about $500.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.120
Healthier, more plant-based,
diets may be about

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.520
25 percent less expensive.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:56.480
And eating groats and greens,

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.880
maybe even spicy
groats and greens,

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.000
may be able to provide
an extra GLP-1 boost.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.760
For more healthy
weight-loss tips,

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.680
check out my evidence-based
weight-loss book,

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:09.920
for which all proceeds I receive
are donated to charity.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.760
The Drug and Therapeutics
Bulletin,

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.000
which is also independent

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.200
and doesn’t accept
any advertising,

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.360
concluded that more data
on Ozempic’s

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.200
long-term safety and efficacy
are needed

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.520
before it can be recommended
for routine use

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.600
for the treatment of obesity,

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.920
reminding readers
that historically,

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.160
nearly all the drugs
approved for weight loss

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.920
have later been
pulled from the market

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.840
because of safety concerns.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.200
But wait.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:36.480
Obesity so dramatically
decreases one’s lifespan

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:37.520
that even if these drugs

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.000
ended up shaving years
off of people’s lives,

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.160
wouldn’t they still be worth it?

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.160
Well, that assumes
these drugs cure obesity,

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.800
but if you remember from
the drug’s own package insert,

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:50.480
in all the major trials,

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.440
people started out obese
and ended up obese,

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.440
after the drugs effectively
stopped working

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.760
and body weight plateaus.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.320
Then, you’re paying to take the
drug for the rest of your life

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.040
just so you don’t lose ground
and re-gain everything,

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.720
while continuing to face any
and all long-term side effects.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.360
Historically, the medical
profession has offered

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.360
a sorry collection of harmful

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.480
or downright dangerous
weight-loss interventions.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:16.400
Caution about
long-term side effects is,

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.080
therefore, warranted.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.120
If you look at
the post-approval withdrawal

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.720
of anti-obesity drugs,

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:25.040
pulled from the market
because of safety concerns

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.880
only discovered years later,

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.440
it took an average of a decade
before dangers came to light,

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.320
and in one case,

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.840
we didn’t discover
a weight-loss drug’s

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:34.960
long-term adverse effects

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:38.400
until 38 years
after it hit the market.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.280
What’s more, even after
that first report of danger,

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.280
it takes an average
of another decade

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.040
to actually get it banned.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.440
It can even take as long as
another two decades,

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:50.320
even though people died
in about a quarter of cases.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:53.920
As one critic said about how
long it takes regulators to act:

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.320
"It would probably
take the system 2 years

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.960
to ban cyanide.”

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:01.760
Just recently,
a French drug maker was fined

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.680
nearly half a billion dollars

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.840
for fraudulently
and relentlessly promoting

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.760
its appetite-suppressing
weight-loss drug

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.840
while covering up known harms,

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:14.400
causing hundreds or thousands to
die from heart valve problems.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.560
At least it learned its lesson,
though.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.320
I mean, what other drug company
would conceal the harms

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.840
of appetite suppressors
after a fine that big?

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:27.520
After all, it was only making up
to 20 million euros a year.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:31.178
Let me do the math real quick...

00:11:31.178 --> 00:11:33.040
That’ll teach ’em!
These days, GLP-1 drug makers

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.200
are worth more
than a trillion dollars.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:39.028
I’m sure they would never try
to cover anything up.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:44.560
Visit nutritionfacts.org/audio to see
all of the podcast episodes

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:48.640
with descriptions that include
links to their associated videos.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.640
